  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "近現代名家書法專題實作",
    "sub_ename": "THEMATIC PRACTICE OF CALLIGRAPHY ON MODERN AND CONTEMPORARY MASTERS",
    "describe_ch": "書法自古以來向有鍾張二王之傳承，以字體言亦各有標舉。迄於現代，名家輩出，惟近人對晚近書家相對陌生，為開拓學生眼界，本課程擬就于右任的草書變革；王福厂的小篆、隸書；沈尹默碑帖融合的楷、行書；董作賓學術成就下的甲骨文書法；臺靜農的藝、境交融等近現代五位書法家的書法表現，了解、臨習、感受其學思歷程，揣摩其意蘊、內涵，來體現新時代變革中由實用轉為藝術表現的書法創作、思考書法文化當代性的構建過程，並有以感悟、形塑自己的生活美學觀。",
    "describe_eh": "Calligraphy has long inherited the traditions of masters like Chong, Chang and Two Wang, with each script style establishing its unique hallmark. In modern times, numerous renowned calligraphers have emerged, yet the pubic are relatively unfamiliar with their works. To broaden students' horizons, this course focuses on the calligraphic innovations of five modern and contemporary calligraphers, for example, Youren’s reforms in cursive script, Wang Fuchang’s contributions to small seal script and clerical script, Shen Yinmo’s integration of stele and model script styles into standard and running scripts, Dong Zuobin’s oracle bone script influenced by his academic achievements, and Tai Jingnong’s synthesis of artistry and mood. By studying, practicing, and experiencing the artistic formation of these calligraphers, students will explore the profound meaning and inner essence of their works. This approach aims to reflect the transformation of calligraphy from practical skills to an art form during periods of significant changes. Furthermore, students will examine the process of constructing contemporary culture in calligraphy, ultimately cultivating the aesthetic perspectives and shaping their sense of artistic beauty in life.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
